meta {
  name: Trigger Webhook
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/hooks/:token
  body: json
  auth: none
}

params:path {
  token: {{triggerToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "event": "lead.created",
    "data": {
      "email": "jane.doe@example.com"
    }
  }
}

docs {
  Delivers a webhook to an active `webhook` trigger, firing its target
  workflow or agent. This is the URL you hand to an external provider.

  No session and no API key — the `{token}` path segment is the entire
  auth story, matched against `triggers.token`. Set `triggerToken` from
  `Triggers/Triggers - Create` or `Triggers - Rotate Token`. Rate
  limited by the `trigger-hooks` throttle.

  Deliberately sits outside the Internal and Public route groups, so it
  inherits neither's middleware.

  Responses are **not** wrapped in the standard envelope:

  - `200 { "status": "accepted" }` — received. Also returned for
    ignored, duplicate, and skipped events on purpose: providers fan
    every event at one URL, and a non-2xx causes retries and eventually
    hook disabling.
  - `401 Invalid signature.` — the trigger has a signing secret and
    verification failed. The rejection is still recorded.
  - `404` — no active webhook trigger matches the token.
}
